---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'

const pageTitle = 'About — analogattention'
const pageDescription =
  'A personal blog about getting your attention back, and what to do with it once you have.'
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class='py-20 sm:py-24 lg:py-28'>
    <div class='mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8'>
      <h1 class='font-serif text-4xl font-light leading-[1.06] tracking-tight sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl'>About</h1>
      <div class='prose mt-10'>
        <p>
          Analog Attention is a blog about getting your attention back, and what to do with it once you have. It
          started with one number; three hours a day on social media adds up to 13.4 years of your conscious life. I
          deleted social media not long after, and these posts are what grew in the gap it left.
        </p>
        <p>
          Expect opinion pieces, not guides. Some are about phones, feeds and algorithms. Some are about travel,
          discomfort, and being your own best friend. Each one starts as notes on my phone and ends as an argument I've
          tried to think through properly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class='prose mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10 [&>h2]:mt-0'>
        <h2>Who writes it</h2>
        <p>
          I'm from Melbourne and I work in tech, which means more of my working day is spent online than I'd like to
          admit. That's probably why this blog exists. I'd rather be on a mountain, at a hostel table, or anywhere the
          phone can stay in my pocket.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm not an expert, and I'm not selling anything; there are no ads and no affiliate links. I write with help
          from AI, and each post says how much. If something here rings true, or doesn't, I'd like to hear about it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
